e secret string to confirm it no longer appears.  \\n   * Test that the new credential works and the old one is invalid.  \\n\\nFollowing these steps removes the secret from every commit in the repo and ensures the compromised credential can no longer be used.\", \"hyperparameters\": null, \"input\": \"What Git steps rewrite history to purge a committed secret and ensure credential revocation?\", \"retrieval_context\": [\"Removing sensitive information from Git history may require history rewriting and credential rotation. If a credential has been exposed, simply deleting the latest copy is not sufficient; the credential itself should generally be revoked or rotated.\\n\\nSigned Commits\\n\\nGit supports commit signing using mechanisms such as GPG and SSH signatures. GitHub can display verification information for supported signed commits. Signing provides a way to establish that a commit was produced by a holder of a particular signing key.\\n\\nSigning does not prove that the code itself is safe or correct. It primarily provides an identity/authenticity signal for the commit.\\n\\nGitHub Dependabot\\n\\nDependabot can help identify and update vulnerable or outdated dependencies. It can create pull requests that update dependency versions according to repository configuration.\\n\\nDependency updates should still be tested because changing a dependency can affect application behavior.\\n\\nGitHub Code Scanning\", \"Removing sensitive information from Git history may require history rewriting and credential rotation. If a credential has been exposed, simply deleting the latest copy is not sufficient; the credential itself should generally be revoked or rotated.\\n\\nSigned Commits\\n\\nGit supports commit signing using mechanisms such as GPG and SSH signatures. GitHub can display verification information for supported signed commits. Signing provides a way to establish that a commit was produced by a holder of a particular signing key.\\n\\nSigning does not prove th